The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

stokes1

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

stokes1a:

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 This is the stokes1 problem with the following changes:
  1) Q1isoQ2 shape functions
  2) subdomain Gauss integration (using 4 subdomains)

stokes1b:

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 This is the stokes1 problem with the following changes:
  1) Exclude p-p zero block from the matrix
  2) timer 

stokes2

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
 Poiseuille flow.
 Collocation of nodes.

stokes3

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions
 Poiseuille flow.
 weak coupling

stokes4

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions
 Poiseuille flow.
 weak coupling. pressure difference via additional unknown.

stokes6

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Two fixed objects.

stokes7

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely translating and rotating object.

stokes8

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.

stokes9

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Sample in single point and sample on a line.

stokes9a:

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Sample in single point and sample on a line.

 This is the stokes9 problem with the following changes:
  1) Q1isoQ2 shape functions
  2) subdomain Gauss integration (using 4 subdomains)

stokes11

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.

stokes11a:

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.

 This is the stokes11 problem with the following changes:
  1) Exclude p-p zero block from the matrix
  2) timer 

stokes12

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely translating and rotating object.
 sparskit solver
 Metis renumbering (commented out)

stokes13

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.

 Output to vtk files

stokes15

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
 Poiseuille flow.
 Collocation of nodes on connecting objects

stokes16

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Tecplot output

stokes17

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Weak constraint on the particle boundary.
 Use of subscript to get constraint data (lagrangian multipliers and
 additional unknowns).

stokes18

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions
 Poiseuille flow.
 weak coupling
 Flow rate imposed using a global constraint on an object
 The position of the constraint can be located at any position
 Flow rate computation in any cross-section using integrate_object

stokes19

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Non-conforming coupling of two domains.

stokes20

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Non-conforming coupling of two domains (vertical velocity)
 Connection of two domains (horizontal velocity, slip layer) using objects.

stokes21

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 integral p dA = 0

stokes22

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.
 integral p dA = 0 using a constraint on a surface

stokes23

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.

 This is the stokes8 problem with P2+/P1^d Crouzeix-Raviart triangles

stokes25

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 Identical to stokes1 but now using a user Gauss rule.
 Uses generalized_stokes elements

stokes26

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 Similar to stokes1 but now:
 Iterative solver with block preconditioning (using pressure mass matrix).

stokes27

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.

 Similar to stokes11 but now:
 Iterative solver using block preconditioning (using pressure mass matrix). 

stokes28

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 Similar to stokes26, but now including a mass matrix with a factor a.

stokes29

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 Similar to stokes28, but now: 
 iterative solver with block preconditioning (using both pressure mass and
 diffusion matrix). M_p^{-1}F_pA_p^{-1} form for inverse Schur complement.

stokes30

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.

 Similar to stokes27, but now including a mass matrix with a factor a and
 iterative solver with block preconditioning (using both pressure mass and
 diffusion matrix). M_p^{-1}F_pA_p^{-1} form for inverse Schur complement.

stokes31

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 Similar to stokes29, but now: M_1^{-1}+M_2^{-1} form for inverse Schur
 complement.

stokes32

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 integral p dA = 0 using a constraint on an elementset

 Similar to stokes21, but now using elementsets.

stokes33

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
 Poiseuille flow.
 Collocation of nodes.

 Similar to stokes2, but now using nodesets instead of curves for the 
 constraint.

stokes34

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Spectral elements.

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with spectral elements.

stokes35

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Stabilized element example: Q2/Q2 velocity/pressure

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with Q2/Q2 elements.

stokes36

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Stabilized element example: P1/P1 velocity/pressure

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with P1/P1 elements.

stokes37

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
 Poiseuille flow.
 Collocation of nodes.
 Stabilized element example: Q1/Q1 velocity/pressure

 This problem is similar to stokes2, but now with Q1/Q1 elements.

stokes38

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Equal order spectral elements.

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with spectral elements having
 equal-order continuous stabilized velocity/pressure Qp/Qp elements 

stokes39

 Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
 Poiseuille flow.
 Collocation of nodes.
 Navier-slip boundary conditions.

stokes40

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Connection of two domains (horizontal velocity, slip layer) using curves.

stokes41

 Stokes problem on a unit square. 
 One-sided connected boundary conditions (collocated).
 Channel flow.
 The velocities on the inflow are set to the velocities on the outflow using
 a connection.

stokes42

 Stokes problem on a rectangular domain with a disk at the center.
 A force and/or torque is applied on the particle.
 Gmsh mesh.
 Interfacial slip on the particle boundary.

stokes43

 Stokes problem on a cubic domain with a sphere at the center.
 A force and/or torque is applied on the particle.
 Gmsh mesh.
 Interfacial slip on the particle boundary.

stokes44

 Axisymmetrical Stokes problem of a sphere at the centerline of a cylindrical 
 container. A force is applied on the particle.
 Gmsh mesh.
 Interfacial slip on the particle boundary.

stokes45

 Stokes problem on a unit square.
 Lid-driven cavity flow with optional Dirichlet or traction free boundary
 condition in normal direction of the lid.
 Arbitrary rotation of mesh.
 Boundary conditions applied using transformations.
 Optional Neumann condition in the transformed system.
 Show various possibilities for applying transformations:
 1) A global vector/matrix valid for each node on the geometry.
 2) A user subroutine called for each node on the geometry.
 3) In the direction of the normal on the geometry.
 Internal subroutine as actual subroutine argument (f2008).

stokes46

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.
 Arbitrary rotation of mesh over the y-axis.
 Boundary conditions applied using transformations.
 Optional Neumann condition in the transformed system.
 Show various possibilities for applying transformations:
 1) A global vector/matrix valid for each node on the geometry.
 2) A user subroutine called for each node on the geometry.
 3) In the direction of the normal on the geometry.
 Internal subroutine as actual subroutine argument (f2008).

stokes47

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 This similar to stokes1, but now with Crouzeix-Raviart Q2/P1 element.
 Global shape functions for pressure.

stokes48

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.
 This similar to stokes11, but now with Crouzeix-Raviart Q2/P1 element.
 Global shape functions for pressure.

stokes49

 Stokes problem on a unit square with 3D velocities (developed flow).
 Lid-driven cavity flow in (x,y).
 Imposed flow rate in z-direction.

stokes51

 Stokes problem on a 3D square cavity. Only half of the domain is solved
 due to symmetry conditions.
 Prisms.

stokes52

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.

 This is stokes1 example with Gauss integration specified by order.
 NOTE: not described in the userguide.

stokes53

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Equal order high-order triangular elements.

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with high-order elements having
 equal-order continuous stabilized velocity/pressure Pp/Pp elements 

stokes54

 Stokes problem on a unit square with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Lid-driven cavity flow.
 Physical quantities.
 Equal order high-order quadrilateral elements.

 This problem is similar to stokes1, but now with high-order elements having
 equal-order continuous stabilized velocity/pressure Qp/Qp elements 
